 6. 🎙️ Rubio&#x27;s greatest podcast hits 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Katie Miller interviews Secretary of State Marco Rubio and his wife, Jeanette Rubio. Screenshot : "The Katie Miller Podcast" Secretary of State Marco Rubio isn't running for president — but his interview on " The Katie Miller Podcast " this week showcased why so many Republicans want him to, Axios' Marc Caputo writes. 

 Why it matters: Miller's show is the Trump administration's go-to new-media outlet where officials talk at length about their personal opinions and lives in a friendly setting. 3 moments from the head-turning interview:

 🛸 UFOs: Rubio nodded to the fact that Miller's husband, deputy White House chief of staff Stephen Miller, has the portfolio overseeing UAPs (Unidentified Anomalous Phenomena).

 Rubio said : "I don't know who it is. I don't know what it is. But there are things flying over our military installation, and they're not ours, and we should look into this." 🥩 RFK's diet: "This is a crazy diet," Rubio said . "He has to travel with coolers full of sauerkraut. I'm not going to travel the world with a cooler full of sauerkraut. It's ridiculous. I can't do it."

 Asked what Rubio eats, his wife replied, "Pop-Tarts." "No," he countered. "I don't eat Pop-Tarts every day. The Pop-Tart is one of the great American innovations in the history of the world." 🐈 Cats: Rubio said the family owns two goldendoodle dogs, and he made clear he's no fan of Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth's cat.

 "I never took Pete for a cat guy," Rubio said. "Oftentimes, I'll get home at night and the cat is just sitting on my porch, and just looks at me like: 'What are you doing here?' ... It's an arrogant cat." More from the interview . 

 
 
