 8. 🏀 1 for the road: Team prices soar 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: Axios research. Chart: Erin Davis and Danielle Alberti/Axios This chart shows the astonishing spike — a literal hockey stick! — in how much professional sports teams have sold for over the last few decades.

 The Los Angeles Lakers were sold yesterday to venture capitalist Josh Kushner and former Disney CEO Bob Iger at an astonishing $12.5 billion valuation — the most ever for a pro sports club. Billionaire Mark Walter reached a deal to buy the controlling stake just last June at a $10 billion valuation, meaning the team's value increased by $2.5 billion in 14 months. Between the lines: The $12.5 billion sale is double the record price for an American sports franchise just three years ago, when the Washington Commanders sold for $6.1 billion.

